Root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect interpretation of the message data structure from the PCAN-USB interface, where the error counter values were mistakenly read from the wrong byte indices (0 and 1) instead of the correct indices (1 and 2). This led to incorrect values being assigned to the receive and transmit error counters.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
pdev->bec.rxerr = mc->ptr[0];
pdev->bec.txerr = mc->ptr[1];
```
Reason:
The error counter values were incorrectly read from the first two bytes of the message data (indices 0 and 1) instead of the correct bytes (indices 1 and 2), leading to incorrect values being assigned to the receive and transmit error counters.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
pdev->bec.rxerr = mc->ptr[1];
pdev->bec.txerr = mc->ptr[2];
```
Reason:
The patch corrects the byte indices from which the error counter values are read, ensuring that the receive and transmit error counters are now assigned the correct values from bytes 1 and 2 of the message data, thus fixing the bug.


